course: dictionary
lesson: 12422
title: Dazed: stunned and confused
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dazed» means unable to think clearly for a short time. You can feel dazed after a bump on the head, a great shock, or when you are very tired. «After the bump, Sam sat on the grass, looking dazed.» The bump is the clue: Sam cannot think straight yet.
explain: The verb «daze» means to make someone confused or stunned. «The bright light dazed him» means the light made him unable to see or think clearly for a moment. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "The bright light made him confused" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Be careful with «dazed». If someone looks dazed after a fall or a bump to the head, tell an adult straight away. It can be a sign of concussion, which needs checking.
explain: Stories use «dazed» for big moments too. «In a daze, Mia walked out of the room after the news.» The phrase «in a daze» means in a stunned, confused state, as if you are not fully awake to what is happening.
fact: «Dazed» means unable to think clearly for a short time.
fact: «Daze» is the verb: «the bright light dazed him» means it made him confused or stunned.
fact: The phrases «in a daze» and «dazed and confused» both describe a stunned, confused state.
fact: If someone is dazed after a bump to the head, tell an adult at once, as it can be a sign of concussion.
fact: A good context clue for «dazed» is a shock, a bump or a surprise just before it.
exercise: «After the bump on the head, Sam sat on the grass, looking dazed.» What does dazed mean here? | *Unable to think clearly for a short time | Cold and wet from the rain | Very happy and full of energy | Running fast and laughing
exercise: «The bright light dazed him.» What does the verb daze mean in this sentence? | Made him laugh loudly | Made him very hungry | Made him run away quickly | *Made him confused or stunned
exercise: «After the news, Mia walked out of the room in a daze.» What does «in a daze» suggest? | Calm and relaxed on a sunny day | *Stunned and confused | Angry and shouting at everyone | Excited and ready for a race
test: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means stunned or confused: «The loud crash left the team dazed for a moment.» | crash | team | *dazed | loud
test: Ben says he feels dazed after bumping his head at football. What should he do? | Hide the bump and say nothing | Run around to clear his head | *Stop playing and tell an adult straight away | Keep playing and forget about it
exam: Which sentence uses «dazed» correctly? | *After the loud bang, the children stood there looking dazed. | She ran a dazed race to win the prize. | The soup was dazed and cold.
